// Feature: first start and the setup wizard. Code: start.sh / start.ps1 (Docker hosts), app/server (ports.js),
// hooks.server.ts (init, setup guard), infra/migrate, services/backups, services/setup, services/settings,
// routes (public)/welcome and (public)/setup.
views {
  dynamic view first_start {
    title 'First start: the port, migrations, backup, the setup wizard'
    description '''
      **A group installs the app and sets it up in the browser, Jellyfin style, without editing files.**

      **Decisions**
      - The port is decided at start, never in the browser. The app tries PORTS in order (default 3000 to 3005)
        and logs each move ("Port 3000 is in use, trying 3001"). If every port is taken it says so and exits 1.
        After a fallback an http ORIGIN with an explicit port is pointed at the opened port for that run; an
        https ORIGIN or one without a port is never touched.
      - With Docker the check runs on the host: ./start.sh (start.ps1 on Windows) creates .env from .env.example
        with a generated database password when it is missing, keeps the port this app's own container already
        publishes, otherwise writes the first free port into APP_PORT (and an http ORIGIN), then runs
        docker compose up -d and waits for /health/ready. A saved port taken by another program moves to the next
        free one with a warning that links changed. Inside the container PORTS=3000, which is always free there.
      - Before any pending migration runs, the app writes a pg_dump to the backups volume (forward-only migrations;
        the dump is the undo). Migrations run in one transaction under an advisory lock; a failure stops the app.
      - Setup is open while no owner exists: every page goes to /welcome and the log says "Setup is open at
        <address>". There is no token. On a shared network the first visitor becomes the owner (accepted risk).
      - The wizard (Owner, Look, Done) checks each step in the browser and posts once. One transaction locks the
        settings row, re-checks that no owner exists, creates the owner, saves text size and accent, marks setup
        done and signs the owner in. A second submit is refused.
      - After setup, /welcome and /setup send people to /login; setup never shows again unless the copy is
        reinstalled.
      - /health/ready answers 503 until migrations are applied; /health/live answers as soon as the process runs.
    '''
    owner -> fl.start 'runs ./start.sh (Docker)'
    fl.start -> fl.app.server 'first free port of PORTS into .env, docker compose up -d (the container: PORTS=3000)'
    fl.app.server -> fl.app.hooks 'listen on the first free port of PORTS (http ORIGIN fixed after a fallback), load the built app'
    fl.app.hooks -> fl.app.services.backupService 'dump before migrating'
    fl.app.hooks -> fl.app.infra 'apply migrations under a lock'
    fl.app.hooks -> fl.app.services.setupService 'no owner: log that setup is open'
    visitor -> fl.app.web.publicPages 'opens any page, lands on /welcome, presses Setup, fills the three steps'
    fl.app.web.publicPages -> fl.app.services.setupService 'finish: owner and look'
    fl.app.services.setupService -> fl.app.repos 'lock settings, insert owner, save settings'
    fl.app.services.setupService -> fl.app.services.authService 'start a session'
    fl.app.services.setupService -> fl.app.services.auditService 'record the first owner'
  }
}
